  "summary": "Derp faces tell daily failures: MS Paint panels as folk diaries.",
  "description": "Rage comics (2008-2014) were the internet's folk-drawing age: four-to-eight-panel MS Paint strips using a shared cast — Trollface, FFFFUUUU Guy, Me Gusta, Forever Alone, Derp & Derpina — to narrate small humiliations and small victories of everyday internet life. The faces were reusable memes with standardized emotional payloads; the grammar (build-up, rage-quit panel, \"le\" epic narration) was community-enforced. Reddit's f7u12 and 4chan bred thousands daily before the format aged into cringe and then into nostalgia. Its legacy: proof that meme templates could function as a distributed comic language, and the direct ancestor of today's Wojak dialogue comics.",
  "culturalContext": "Rage comics were the internet's folk-drawing age: shared faces told daily failures in MS Paint panels, the format aged into cringe then nostalgia, and its template logic — reusable emotion as comic language — is the direct ancestor of Wojak culture and today's meme-dialogue comics.",
